  "description": "Roslyn analyzer for Unity C# that flags allocations in hot paths - new objects, hidden allocations such as strings, closures, LINQ (including LINQ-style extension methods), boxing, iterator and async state machines and boxed foreach enumerators, and allocating Unity APIs, outside Burst-compiled code - reports Unity job structs holding managed fields, native containers (NativeArray, NativeList, ...) that are not disposed on every path, and Resources.Load and Addressables loads in hot paths, and offers code fixes that route object allocations through an object pool - writing the pool class when none exists - rent local arrays from ArrayPool<T>.Shared inside a try/finally, and rewrite closures, delegates, string interpolation, simple LINQ chains, tag comparisons, GetComponents calls and Input.touches into cached, reused or non-allocating forms, minimizing GC and frame hitches. Includes a source generator that writes the pool class itself from an [ObjectPool] attribute, and a suppressor that stays quiet for allocations behind a first-frame guard, an editor-only region, a static latch or a field assignment. Configurable from .editorconfig, with a warning for misspelled options.",
  "developmentDependency": true,
